From: lunatickochiya <125438787@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dae: drop bundled go-mod before OpenWrt Go build

dae-full-src.zip carries a pre-populated Go module cache under go-mod/.
OpenWrt's golang-package build copies every *.go file into .go_work,
so "go list github.com/daeuniverse/dae/..." also scans paths such as
go-mod/github.com/davecgh/go-spew@v.../spew. Go rejects those paths
("can only use path@version syntax with 'go get'/'go install'") and the
build fails with "no Go files in .../.go_work/build".

Remove the bundled module cache after extraction; the OpenWrt build uses
its own GOMODCACHE and can fetch the modules normally.

---
--- a/dae/Makefile
+++ b/dae/Makefile
@@ -33,6 +33,13 @@
 
 UNZIP_CMD:=unzip -q -d $(PKG_BUILD_DIR) $(DL_DIR)/$(PKG_SOURCE)
 
+define Build/Prepare
+	$(call Build/Prepare/Default)
+	# OpenWrt copies every *.go file into .go_work; the bundled module
+	# cache contains path@version directories that go list rejects.
+	rm -rf $(PKG_BUILD_DIR)/go-mod
+endef
+
 define Package/dae/Default
   SECTION:=net
   CATEGORY:=Network
